From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn-patches <tyn-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:18:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: downscale textures exceeding GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

可向上游提交。

Mobile GPUs with GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE == 4096 reject textures such as
3072x6000 FONT.PNG and 3072x4224 ALBUM_THUM.DDS with GL_INVALID_VALUE in
glTexImage2D, causing missing or corrupted rendering.

Query GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE in Renderer::Init() (falling back to 4096 if <= 0)
and log GL_RENDERER, GL_VERSION and GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE. In SubmitTexture(),
keep the zero-overhead path when width <= MaxTextureSize and
height <= MaxTextureSize; otherwise downscale only the exceeding axes with
area averaging across TexFmt_RGBA/RGB/UA8/U8 to preserve thin glyph strokes,
log a warning, and check glGetError() after glTexImage2D and glGenerateMipmap.

SpriteSheet::DesignWidth/DesignHeight and GetSpriteSheetImage are unaffected
because sprites and SingleSheetFont sample via NormalizedBounds() in [0, 1].

Verified on MuMu emulator (Android 15, not a real device) with both native
limit and simulated 4096 clamp on steins;gate (sg-pc, Steam + 2018 CN patch).

diff --git a/src/renderer/opengl/renderer.cpp b/src/renderer/opengl/renderer.cpp
index 6facf51015adef23b35f1d3a96e9ca9a4ad8453c..2e3932313da1ae7223e5a5d317a30b0ed667ace8 100644
--- a/src/renderer/opengl/renderer.cpp
